User Rate Limiting
-----------------
Making too many login requests within a short period of time causes our IP address to be blocked.
Typically, the IP can onlyl be unblocked in one of teh following ways:
- Automatically after a certain period of time has elapsed
- Manually by an administrator
- Manually by the user after successfully completing a CAPTCHA
As the limit is based on the rate of HTTP requests sent from the user's IP address, it is sometimes also possible ot bypass this defense if we can work out how to guess multiple passwords with a single request.

Bypassing this can also be done by using multi-credential requests. Some login endpoints rate-limit by number of requests, not number of credentials tried. If the backend accepts a JSON array for the password field (e.g. {"username":"carlos","password":["pass1","pass2",...]}), you can smuggle dozens of guesses into a single request and bypass lockout/throttling entirely, since it only counts as one attempt.
